{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAH9nPVQri63iVVqvCNa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted index 2 (Sb fraction 0.164) as the best composition. It gave the highest EQE I measured, 0.135%.\n\nI used all 5 EQE measurements and none of the XRD budget:\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0.123 | 0.107 |\n| **2** | **0.164** | **0.135** |\n| 6 | 0.274 | 0.052 |\n| 13 | 0.493 | 0.010 |\n| 21 | 0.725 | −0.005 |\n\nEQE is best at the iron-rich end and falls off as antimony increases. At Sb fractions of 0.49 and above the films are close to inactive. Index 2 beat both of its measured neighbours, so the peak is probably between Sb ≈ 0.12 and 0.27.\n\nIndices 1, 3, 4 and 5 fall in that range and were never measured. One of them could be slightly better than index 2, so I can't be sure index 2 is the best on the whole line. I used the measurements to find where the peak is rather than to narrow down its exact position.\n\nWith no XRD, I have no phase evidence for why the iron-rich films do better. My guess is that they're mostly Fe₂O₃, which absorbs light at 2.4 eV, but I didn't test that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":498,"cache_read_input_tokens":7126,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":498},"output_tokens":437,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"258d4684-be9f-4dbf-9a4f-31953728293e","uuid":"7a9cc32d-c222-46e1-b918-f45d8b809db2","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:32:39.297Z","request_id":"req_011CfAH9mwhkrfLbu2j9un57"}
